smd: 2
title: Display math delimiters in spec v2
summary: "Pins how spec v2 reads `$$` display math (RFC proposal 2): it opens on a line that is only `$$`, or `$$…$$` on one line, and closes on a line that is only `$$`. Read with `smd: 1`, a line that starts or ends with `$$` is a delimiter; the unit tests compare both."
status: draft
updated: 2026-10-17
---

## Own-line delimiters

The area of a circle:

$$
A = \pi r^2
$$

$$ E = mc^2 $$

## Text beside a delimiter

Pricing:
$$5 per seat, billed monthly

## Plans

The team plan costs $$

The line that starts with `$$` and the line that ends with `$$` are text in spec v2: no math opens or closes on them, and the heading between them is a heading.

## Math in a callout

:::note Ratios
$$
\frac{a}{b}
:::
\frac{c}{d}
$$

Still inside the note: math is opaque, so the `:::` line in it is math.
:::

Outside the note.
